    "time_horizon": "immediate",
    "confidence": "moderate",
    "plain": "Cutting foreign aid by 50% would free up around \u00a36 billion of public spending, directly reducing the deficit and improving the near-term fiscal position. The main caveat is that the government has already committed to significant aid reductions, so the genuinely additional saving may be smaller than \u00a36 billion.",
    "biggest_unknown": "How much of the claimed \u00a36 billion saving is genuinely additional given the government has already committed to reducing aid to 0.3% of GNI by 2027, which itself implies a roughly \u00a36 billion reduction from 2023 levels.",
